# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# This file was called _headers.txt and therefore did nothing. Pages reads
# `_headers`, no extension, so every rule below had never been applied: a live
# check showed no Content-Security-Policy, no Strict-Transport-Security, no
# X-Frame-Options and no Permissions-Policy, and /data/*.json being served with
# Pages' default `max-age=0, must-revalidate` rather than the 300s intended
# here. The two headers that were present, nosniff and Referrer-Policy, are
# Pages defaults and arrive with or without this file.
#
# The CSP below was audited against what the site actually loads before being
# switched on, because a wrong one fails closed and breaks the page:
#
#   script-src   cdn.jsdelivr.net (Chart.js) and unpkg.com (lucide, injected at
#                runtime by common.js). 'unsafe-inline' is not optional: there
#                are 333 inline onclick= handlers and ~14.6k lines of inline
#                <script>. No eval or new Function anywhere, so 'unsafe-eval'
#                is deliberately absent.
#   connect-src  the FPL proxy worker; api.rss2json.com for the news feeds;
#                docs.google.com for the Season Vault CSV export; and
#                pulselive for shirt numbers — that last one is fetched from
#                team-analysis-core.js and index.html and was missing from the
#                original policy, so enabling the file as written would have
#                broken jersey numbers on two pages.
#   img-src      https: covers the Premier League badge CDN.
#   font-src     Google Fonts, plus 'self' for anything served locally later.
#
# No iframes and no <form> elements exist on the site, so frame-ancestors,
# form-action and object-src are locked down rather than left to default-src.
#
# Two things only a real page load could reveal, both found with devtools open:
#
#   Cloudflare Web Analytics injects static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js
#   at the edge, so it appears in no file in this repo and in no curl of the
#   origin. It needs script-src for the beacon AND connect-src for the RUM POST
#   it then makes to cloudflareinsights.com — allowing only the first would have
#   loaded the script and blocked its payload, producing a second violation
#   instead of a fix. Analytics had been silently dead since the rename.
#
#   Source maps are fetched under connect-src, not script-src, so unpkg and
#   jsdelivr appear in both. This only bites with devtools open, but a console
#   full of CSP noise is how a real violation gets missed.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' https: data:; connect-src 'self' https://fpl-proxy.jguilhermealexandre.workers.dev https://api.rss2json.com https://docs.google.com https://sdp-prem-prod.premier-league-prod.pulselive.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# The data feed is rewritten every 15 minutes during match windows, so 300s at
# the edge is roughly one refresh behind at worst and takes the repeated reads
# off the origin entirely. Without this rule these were cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC
# — every visitor fetching every file from origin, on the hottest paths on the
# site.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=300
